  "confirmedStaticContract": [
    "Menu favorite NewBookmarkUserAction opens a separate INewBookmarkPage and updates header menu bookmark state only after callback. It is not the voucher-bookmark action.",
    "Voucher list selection is cloned from selected row data; input context takes the current DMC record. A zero-selection path alerts and stops.",
    "For list models, FilterDeleteStatusProgram supplies pass/fail groups; invalid-key notice close/negative confirmation or no valid records stops before sending. Server acceptance remains unverified.",
    "Voucher request keys include date/no, business/menu IDs and fixed blank secondary/document IDs/type0. The send call delegates persistence to ISendSlipToInsideBookmarkAction with program/menu metadata.",
    "The send/persistence action is awaited before openBookmark asks whether to open the list page. The confirmation controls subsequent opening, not the earlier save; do not click as a supposedly read-only popup probe.",
    "The open message reads is_bookmark_saved and bookmark_max_cnt and passes literal100 to a localized message. This does not prove a universal100-item or total storage policy."
  ],
  "currentImplementation": "Deployed menu favorite toggleFavorite/cleanState stores valid menu IDs only (cleanState limits menu favorites/recent to50); this is not voucher/bookmark persistence and no voucher bookmark feature is claimed.",
  "remaining": [
    "Official manual014 full body and actual non-writing bookmark-list navigation/read/filter/persistence contract.",
    "ISendSlipToInsideBookmarkAction server behavior and the bookmark list page are absent; duplicate handling, maximum counts, lifetime, permissions/company/user isolation, stale/deleted documents, remove/restore and partial-failure policy are unverified.",
    "Actual voucher bookmark versus menu favorite labels/location and document read-link behavior; do not implement either by relabeling existing menu-star storage.",
    "Original send/bookmark creation is a write; skip its action during source observation even after authorized login. Only use verified read-only entry paths."
  ],
